course: dictionary
lesson: 10112
title: One more than twelve
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Thirteen is a number. It is written 13, and it is one more than twelve. When you count on from twelve, the next number you say is thirteen.
explain: Thirteen can also mean a group of things. A baker's dozen is 13, so it is one more than the usual dozen of twelve. Look at the words around the number to see what it counts.
explain: Context helps with numbers too. «Her sums go wrong» tells you a sum can be wrong, so always check the number is right. «Ella turned thirteen this year» tells you she is now a teenager, because thirteen-year-olds are teenagers.
fact: Thirteen means the number 13, one more than twelve.
fact: A baker's dozen means 13.
fact: 13 is a prime number, because only 1 and itself divide it exactly.
fact: Some people think 13 is unlucky, but that is only a superstition, not a fact.
fact: «Some American cicadas spend thirteen or seventeen years underground before coming out together.»
exercise: What number comes straight after twelve? | Twenty | *Thirteen | Eleven | Fourteen
exercise: A baker's dozen is how many? | Twelve | Fourteen | *Thirteen | Twenty
exercise: «Ella turned thirteen this year.» What is Ella now? | Eleven years old | *A teenager | A baby | A grown-up of twenty
test: Thirteen is one more than which number? | Eleven | *Twelve | Fourteen | Ten
test: Why is 13 called a prime number? | It is the smallest number | *Only 1 and itself divide it exactly | It is a multiple of ten | It is an even number
exam: Read: «Some people think 13 is unlucky, but that is only a superstition.» What does superstition mean? | *A belief that is not based on fact | A large number | A kind of cake | A type of sum
